WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.020
There are many mysteries locked within the
walls of the SCP Foundation, from potentially

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.990
world-ending scenarios to the minds of monsters
like the hard-to-destroy reptile.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:16.080
Day after day, the research staff work tirelessly
to unravel these secrets, contain them, and,

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.070
when necessary, terminate them.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:23.199
But what about another researcher, another
man of science trying desperately to uncover

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:24.199
the truth?

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.640
Today, we put down the clipboards and white
lab coats in favor of black robes, a beaked

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.829
mask - or rather, skull - and a seemingly
endless doctor's bag, to take a look at the

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:42.610
average day for one peculiar physician: SCP-049,
The Plague Doctor.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:48.450
We took the liberty of turning the researcher
into the research subject, watching SCP-049

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:54.550
as he went about his daily life, from his
inscrutable experiments to his strange habits.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.350
It was difficult to chronicle without tipping
the good Doctor off as to what we were up

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.719
to, but we were able to get everything we
needed to make the video you’re watching

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:03.750
right now.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:10.369
Welcome, friends, enemies, and future patients,
to a Day In The Life of SCP-049.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.700
6:00 AM

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.749
The Great Dying never sleeps, and neither,
really, does the Plague Doctor.

00:01:16.749 --> 00:01:21.200
Unlike ordinary human doctors, he does not
need to get his eight hours of shuteye in

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.039
order to function properly.

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:28.520
The sharp mind of SCP-049 never dulls, no
matter how long he is awake.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.369
Of course, he does occasionally lie down in
his containment cell, arms crossed over his

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:38.180
chest like a mummy, breathing at a noticeably
slower pace for several hours.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:43.409
However, he does not appear to actually enter
a REM cycle, nor does his behavior change

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:45.630
when he is denied this rest time.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.739
It would appear he is simply, for lack of
a better term, brainstorming for a little

00:01:49.739 --> 00:01:52.969
while before getting up to start the new day.

00:01:52.969 --> 00:01:57.459
Back when he lived on the outside, he would
rise to the sound of a rooster's crow or the

00:01:57.459 --> 00:02:01.890
ringing of church bells in the town square,
but now, we discovered, the Plague Doctor

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.149
becomes active for the day at exactly 6:00
AM, on the dot.

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:10.399
We're not sure how he manages such precision,
since there are no clocks visible from his

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:14.489
room, but then again there's a lot we still
don't understand about him.

00:02:14.489 --> 00:02:19.379
But whether you wake to the sound of a buzzing
phone alarm or your own perfectly tuned internal

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:24.730
clock, there's nothing wrong with getting
a nice early start on your day's tasks!

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.790
Just like he doesn't need sleep, the Plague
Doctor does not rely on steady caloric intake

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.010
for his energy.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:34.019
Instead, he is sustained by the satisfaction
of doing what needs to be done.

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:36.849
But that doesn't mean he can't eat!

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:41.560
He enjoys starting the day with breakfast,
often consisting of toasted bread with butter,

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.719
jam, or honey.

00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:46.439
If he's feeling particularly indulgent, sometimes
all three!

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:51.859
And he washes it down with an espresso or
a cup of steaming hot lavender tea.

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:56.090
Though he's a serious man, he understands
the importance of treating yourself first

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.379
thing in the morning.

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:02.250
It sets the tone for the day, and gives him
the boost he'll need for what's to come.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.480
8:00 AM

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.000
Some people enjoy a long, languid morning
routine.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.810
They shower, they do their eleven-step skincare
regimen, they do some gentle stretching to

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.780
wake up their muscles and circular system.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.010
SCP-049 is not one of those people.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.430
He is a no muss no fuss type, through and
through.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:25.139
Besides, with gloves, robes, and a mask that
are parts of his physical body, it's uncertain

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:30.139
if he has any skin that really needs caring
for, or produces sweat that might need to

00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:31.499
be washed away.

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:36.900
We're not sure if you can use Korean sheet
masks on chitin, but we don't think the Plague

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.150
Doctor would let us try.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:44.730
With no hygiene to worry about, it's time
for SCP-049 to get going on his favorite activity,

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:51.340
the one that borders on all-encompassing obsession:
working toward a cure for the Great Dying,

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:55.540
the pestilence that he has devoted his existence
to fighting.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:04:00.319
Once upon a time, the Foundation was so kind
as to offer him corpses to experiment on.

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:04.870
But, given the Doctor's penchant for resurrecting
the dead and turning them into mindless zombies

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:10.230
that follow his every command, they decided
to do away with that particular program.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:15.019
You can't always get what you want, especially
when what you want results in an army of the

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:16.120
undead.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.959
Living test subjects won't work either, between
his deadly touch and his tendency toward,

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:26.490
shall we say, unconventional surgical methods,
it's just not the best idea.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.750
So, what's a Doc to do?

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.400
His best with what he's got, of course.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:36.199
Around this time of morning, he sets up a
neat row of tools and implements on his favorite

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:42.090
workbench, and selects various tissue samples
to dissect, to inject with solutions and dissolve

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:49.120
in jars, to study from every angle he can
until he finally cracks the cure to the Pestilence.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.120
10:00 AM

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:54.620
The work may be his top priority, but no man
is an island!

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.860
Even a man who isn't quite human needs to
engage in polite conversation.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.520
We do still live in a society, after all.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.500
After working in silence for a couple of hours,
the Plague Doctor has gotten into the habit

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.319
of talking to whoever happens to be passing
by his containment facility.

00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:13.870
Sometimes it's a custodian, mopping up bloodstains.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:18.449
Sometimes it's a doctor he can engage with
about their mutual love of science and research.

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:23.680
Sometimes, it's another SCP, one of the lucky
few permitted to roam about the facility without

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.880
much supervision.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:31.640
Today, it was SCP-507, the Reluctant Dimension
Hopper, back from his latest involuntary travel

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.990
to another world.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.030
He was wearing a pair of cargo shorts and
a t-shirt emblazoned with a variety of comic

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.440
book characters.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:43.849
He approached the window of SCP-049's containment
cell with a cheerful wave.

00:05:43.849 --> 00:05:44.849
"Hey Doc!

00:05:44.849 --> 00:05:45.849
How's it going?"

00:05:45.849 --> 00:05:46.849
He smiled.

00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:47.849
"Ah hello!"

00:05:47.849 --> 00:05:49.729
The Doctor's eyes shone excitedly from the
depths of his mask.

00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:51.500
"How nice it is to see you!

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.740
I am having a most productive day - And you,
how did you fare on your voyage?

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:59.250
You are looking well, I presume it was successful?"

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.880
The Plague Doctor wasn't entirely sure what
this friendly man got up to when he was away

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.710
from the Foundation.

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:09.090
Perhaps he was a merchant, or a cartographer
charting foreign lands.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:12.810
One of the white-coated scientists had attempted
to explain it to him, but was called away

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.720
by more important affairs before he could
have his questions answered.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.240
SCP-507 shuddered at the question.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.650
"Not my favorite."

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.120
His face paled at the memory.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:27.870
"I don't want to get into it too much, but
I'll say this: spiders.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.830
Lots and lots of spiders."

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.070
"I'm quite sorry to hear that.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.680
May your next destination be a better one!"

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.800
SCP-507's frown dissolved into a grin at the
Doctor's words.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:39.900
"Appreciate it, Doc.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.370
We'll see, I guess.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:45.539
I'm gonna go ask God some questions about
what happens when we die, good luck with the

00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:46.539
science stuff!"

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:50.530
He pressed a palm to the glass, inviting the
Plague Doctor to give him a high five through

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.530
the window.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:55.680
Haltingly, a bit confused about the gesture,
the Doctor pressed his hand to the glass in

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.680
return.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.759
"See ya around!"

00:06:57.759 --> 00:06:58.759
"Indeed!"

00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:03.689
The Doctor waved as the friendly blond man
headed off to explore his own mortality, and

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.169
probably make a smoothie.
12:00 PM

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:09.669
Right at noon, the Doctor pauses his work
to enjoy a nice lunch.

00:07:09.669 --> 00:07:13.800
Like all of his meals, his food is delivered
through a slot in the door.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:18.930
His lunch consists most often of a wedge of
hard cheese, a small bunch of grapes, and

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.400
some goose liver pate with crackers.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.490
Frequently he will ask to join the staff and
other freely-moving anomalies in the cafeteria,

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:29.360
but due to safety concerns he is not permitted
to do so.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.400
The last thing we need is him brushing hands
with someone while reaching for an extra scoop

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.740
of mashed potatoes and them dropping dead
right there on the tile floor.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:42.620
Still, it's lonely for him to eat in there,
watching the rest of the staff walk to lunch,

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:46.689
gabbing about their weekends and discussing
what the soup of the day might be.

00:07:46.689 --> 00:07:50.729
On this day, the Plague Doctor was having
an especially frustrating lunch.

00:07:50.729 --> 00:07:55.599
As he nibbled delicately on his cheese, he
heard a twinkling melody in the distance.

00:07:55.599 --> 00:07:58.560
Very very faint, coming from somewhere outside.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.659
Suddenly, there was a flurry of activity in
the hall as Foundation employees made their

00:08:02.659 --> 00:08:04.389
way toward the source of the music.

00:08:04.389 --> 00:08:05.720
"Excuse me?"

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.449
He called to a passing security guard.

00:08:07.449 --> 00:08:09.210
"What is all the commotion about?"

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.259
"Dr. Bright stole an ice cream truck!

00:08:11.259 --> 00:08:12.889
Free ice cream for everyone!"

00:08:12.889 --> 00:08:14.490
The woman cried giddily.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.419
"Marvelous, what a treat!

00:08:16.419 --> 00:08:18.360
Might I request you procure a cup for me to-"

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:22.509
But before he could finish his question, she
was already gone, yelling "Don't take all

00:08:22.509 --> 00:08:24.880
the strawberry before I get there!"

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:29.300
SCP-049 watched, beak pressed against the
glass as a parade of people walked past carrying

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:35.290
cones, ice cream bars, bowls piled high with
ice cream scoops, hot fudge, nuts, and cherries.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:40.030
It seemed like everyone was enjoying their
ice cream, cooling down on a hot day with

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:43.040
a sweet treat, except for him.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.700
Even some of the other SCPs were getting in
on the fun.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:52.470
SCP-999 oozed by the door, holding a chocolate
vanilla swirl cone, a sundae, and a chocolate-covered

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.890
frozen banana.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.950
It paused at the sight of the Doctor's sad
expression, making an inquisitive gurgling

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:58.950
sound.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.600
"Good afternoon, dear creature.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.460
It seems I've been left out of the festivities."

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.880
The Plague Doctor sighed.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.030
The Tickle Monster gurgled again, sliding
over to the slot in the door.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.500
"What are you..."

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.770
He trailed off, as the slimy little friend
eased the slot open, and pushed the sundae

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:15.880
and plastic spoon inside.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:19.810
The sundae spilled a little bit on its way
in, but remained mostly intact.

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:20.910
"Thank you!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.380
I am ever in your debt!"

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:24.920
The Plague Doctor exclaimed.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:29.310
The Tickle Monster was already departing,
off to brighten someone else's day.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:30.420
No matter.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.780
Someone had remembered him, and for once he
didn't mind being prohibited from eating in

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.090
the canteen.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.670
Even from his cell, he was still a part of
things.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:40.970
1:30 PM

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:45.830
Every so often, the Plague Doctor experiences
a joyous break in his routine: he is given

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.250
a test subject.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:52.170
Not a human subject, of course, or even a
living subject, but a fresh organic specimen

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.170
nonetheless.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:58.220
As a reward for good behavior, and incentive
to continue cooperating with the Foundation

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:05.130
staff, SCP-049 is occasionally given a deceased
animal specimen to dissect and experiment

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.130
on.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:11.540
In this particular case, it was a large adult
cow that I'm told passed away from natural

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.820
causes after a life of grazing happily in
the sun.

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:19.660
As the cow's body was wheeled into his containment
cell by a group of researchers clad in Hazmat

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:23.810
suits, the Plague Doctor clapped his gloved
hands together excitedly.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:27.380
One of the researchers leaned over to another
and whispered, "I thought this was for sloppy

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.380
joe day?"

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.650
His colleague solemnly shook his head.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.820
"Here you go, Doctor!"

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.820
Another piped up.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.820
"Marvelous!

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.570
Thank you, gentlemen, thank you!"

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.820
SCP-049 exclaimed.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:43.450
He was so overcome with delight that he patted
one of the researchers on the back.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:48.140
The man tensed for a moment, terrified at
the sudden physical contact, but relaxed when

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:52.360
he remembered that his protective gear protected
him from the deadly effects of a touch from

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:54.270
the Plague Doctor.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.510
"Yeah, you got it buddy."

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.060
The man let out a sigh of relief, heart still
racing.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:01.700
"Are you feeling quite alright, my friend?"

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:05.160
The Doctor cocked his head to the side, watching
the man's face closely.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.060
"You seem troubled, perhaps I should provide
you with a cursory examination?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.470
I would hate to see my benefactor fall ill..."

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:16.140
"I'm fine, just a little tired!

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:19.020
Lots to do, can't stay, gotta get to the next
thing!"

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.020
The man laughed nervously.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:21.350
"Come on, let's go."

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:23.680
He hissed to his colleagues, rushing toward
the exit.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.170
They followed, never taking their eyes off
of the Plague Doctor as they went.

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:31.630
"History will remember your contribution to
the advancement of medical science."

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:35.970
The Doctor said solemnly, waving goodbye to
the men as they left and resealed the door

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:36.970
to the room.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.190
4:00 PM

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:39.430
"Eureka!"

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:40.610
Cried the Plague Doctor, and he thrust the
heart back into the cow's chest.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:45.190
After a moment, its eyes opened, and it let
out a warped, strange "mooing" sound that

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:47.080
echoed down the halls.

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:51.570
It stumbled to its feet, milky eyes rolling
around in its head as it took its first breath

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:53.300
since it passed away.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:57.890
The cow had been brought back to life, but,
like all of the patients the Doctor had successfully

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:01.170
cured so far, it was not quite right.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:04.190
It swelled and bulged in strange places.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:08.650
Black slime dribbled from its nostrils and
mouth, and it shuffled around the small room

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:11.760
aimlessly, waiting for guidance.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.940
As it locked eyes with the researcher walking
past, looking at it through the glass, it

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:21.120
let out another moo, chomping its teeth in
anticipation of a bite.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:25.960
Like anyone else briefed on the containment
procedures for SCP-049, this man knew that

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.980
any resurrections were strictly off-limits
for the anomaly.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:33.480
No matter how proud the Plague Doctor was
of his little project for the day, he could

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.160
not be allowed to keep it.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:37.820
It would be confiscated, and terminated.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:42.600
He called for his supervisor, and soon a group
of armed guards was bursting through the door,

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.170
tipping the zombie cow on its side like a
group of rural teens on a rowdy night out.

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:50.430
All the while, the Plague Doctor shouted at
them, "How dare you?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.510
Unhand her immediately!"

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:54.010
But the guards did not listen.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:58.270
They injected the cow with enough tranquilizers
to knock out a herd of elephants, and hauled

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.490
it out of the room toward the incinerator.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:05.670
Alone in his room, the Plague Doctor sat with
his head in his hands, making the sound of

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:09.340
crying, though no tears could be seen running
down his masked face.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.050
"We talked about this, Doctor."

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.390
A Senior Researcher spoke to him through the
window.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.590
"You can't have reanimated corpses in your
cell.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:17.620
It's a security concern."

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:20.680
"She was my first breakthrough in months!"

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.170
He wailed.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:25.680
With a sigh, the Senior Researcher pressed
a button to aid in calming the distressed

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:26.880
anomaly down.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:31.160
A hissing sound filled the containment cell,
as the scent of fresh French lavender was

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.950
pumped into the space.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:37.140
The Doctor lifted his head, taking a deep
breath, and slowly relaxing his shoulders.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.160
"Very well.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.470
Please do me one favor, my friend?

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.680
Bring me her brain?"

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.180
"I can do that."

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:45.510
The Senior Researcher nodded.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:50.670
"But you can't do this again, or we'll have
to revoke your test subject privileges again."

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:52.970
"My work is not a privilege, it is a calling.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.070
A necessity!"

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:57.700
The Doctor pounded a gloved fist on the floor.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:59.520
"Right, of course.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.100
Let me get that brain for you."

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:02.140
7:00 PM

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:06.450
Sometime mid-evening, the Plague Doctor's
meal slot opens again as his dinner is pushed

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.240
through for him to enjoy.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:13.821
Today's supper is roasted potatoes and onions,
a cut of baked fish, more crusty bread, and

00:14:13.821 --> 00:14:16.530
a small cup of fragrant red wine.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:21.260
On special occasions, he is even able to request
a second glass of wine to wash down the troubles

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.460
of the day.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:26.770
After the cow incident, this is not one of
those days, so he drinks his one allotted

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:30.680
cup slowly, savoring it along with his food.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:34.961
Most culinary enthusiasts would suggest against
red wine with fish, but the Plague Doctor

00:14:34.961 --> 00:14:37.450
does not live by the rules of man.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:38.790
He makes his own.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:39.870
8:00 PM

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:45.030
After his dinner, SCP-049 begins tidying his
workspace, preparing to wind down for the

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.030
night.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:50.100
He wipes down his work table, clearing it
of blood, sweat, and other mysterious liquids.

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:54.780
He returns his various tools to their home
in his doctor's bag, sealing the lids on his

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.270
jars and placing them back inside.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.540
He works hard, but one cannot work all the
time.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.620
Rest, taking the time for deep thought and
processing all that he has learned throughout

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:06.820
the day, is just as vital.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:07.980
10:00 PM

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:12.360
To end the day, the Plague Doctor engages
in one of his few simple pleasures: he reads.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:17.290
He has requested, and been provided, various
texts from the Foundation ranging from the

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.990
medical to the literary.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:24.770
He has a compendium of the writings of Hippocrates,
Pliny the Elder's texts of medicine and natural

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:28.590
science, as well as some modern scientific
texts he has largely disregarded.

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:33.730
For lighter reading, he has set aside the
Canterbury Tales, Lady Chatterly's Lover,

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.850
The Lover by Marguerite Duras, and Madame
Bovary.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:41.170
It seems that, when it comes to his fiction,
The Plague Doctor has a bit of a romantic

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.170
side.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:46.460
He lies on his back, reading by the overhead
light, listening as the sounds of the Foundation

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.100
quiet down for the night.

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:52.950
The once-bustling facility now has only the
occasional footsteps, the sounds of doors

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:57.510
closing and machinery being powered down,
as those who can go home to their lives on

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:58.950
the outside, do.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:02.080
But SCP-049 is not one of them.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:07.280
He has always lived for the science, for the
work, and now he lives in a research facility

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.430
full-time.

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:13.720
It may not be an ideal life, but he has found
a way to made do with it, and tomorrow he

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:19.130
will go up against his greatest enemy, the
illness he has sworn to cure, once again.

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:23.100
And there you have it, folks, a day in the
life of the mysterious masked physician.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:26.730
Is there anything from the Plague Doctor's
daily routine that you think you might start

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.310
incorporating into your own day-to-day lives?

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:30.920
Let us know down in the comments.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:36.230
Sometimes, no matter how distant success may
seem, we just have to keep working toward

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:37.230
our goals.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:42.800
No one exemplifies that better than the oh-so-determined
SCP-049, and his tireless attempts to rid

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.370
the world of the Pestilence once and for all.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:49.640
Sure, his methods aren't always the most helpful,
but everybody makes mistakes.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:52.690
The most important thing is to try your best.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:59.150
Now go check out “When Day Breaks SCP-049”
and “Kidnapped by SCP-049” for more tales

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:01.200
about everyone's favorite masked Doctor!

